    This shows that the upper bound in Eq.~\eqref{eq:upperbound} cannot always be achieved. 
    However in Appendix~\ref{sec:constructcoherent}, we show that it is always asymptotically achieved: given basin sizes $n_1,\ldots,n_k$, there exists a network $G$ with coherence $\psi_{G}$, such that  
    % For the rest of this section, we show that even though the upper bound for coherence in equation \eqref{eq:upperbound} is not tight, it is asymptotically tight. \todo{Is this readable?}

    %In particular, as we show in \Cref{theorem:mprasymptotics}, it is always possible to construct a network $\mc{N}^{\prime}$ with coherence asymptotically given by 

