The closed-form expression for the quantum uncommon information is not yet known. Although several studies have investigated specific instances~\cite{Lee2019QSE, Lee2019QSE2, Lee2021QSE}, for the general case, only upper and lower bounds have been established~\cite{Jon2008QUI, Lee2024QUI}.

In this work, we address this gap by proposing a method for predicting bounds on the quantum uncommon information of a given quantum state. Our approach leverages quantum machine learning techniques based on the quantum Donsker--Varadhan representation~\cite{Shin2024QMINE}, which we employ to estimate the von Neumann entropy. These entropy estimates then enable the derivation of corresponding bounds on the quantum uncommon information.


