    \includegraphics[scale=0.325]{Figures/dpflow_msd0.PNG}
    \caption{(a) Time evolution of the mean-squared displacement (divided by 6) of the solvent molecules. The time and MSD are indicated in $\tau_0$ and $\ell_0^2$ unit, respectively.
    (b) Velocity profile obtained from the Poiseuille flow simulation (circles). The coordinate $z$ and the velocity are indicated in $\ell_0$ and $\ell_0/\tau_O$ units, respectively. The line is a fit using  Eq.~\eqref{eq:dpflow}. The computational domain here is \((L_x\times L_y\times L_z)=(10\times 100\times 100)\ell_0^3\). }
