\begin{abstract}
% Economic complexity algorithms, such as the Economic Complexity Index (ECI) and the Non-Homogeneous Economic Fitness and Complexity (NHEFC), are successful tools for capturing the intricate dynamics of economic systems. 
% In this work, we offer a novel perspective on these algorithms by demonstrating that they can be reformulated as optimization problems, each minimizing a specific cost function. 
