We aim to further explore the leverage effect and its implications. As noted in Section~\ref{sec::Empirical App}, while the leverage effect in the LHAR model improves the fit, the associated coefficients exhibit low $t$-statistics, with the monthly component being particularly insignificant. We opted for negative leverage as it demonstrates superior in-sample statistics compared to positive leverage, as shown in Table~(\ref{tab:Lev1}).\\
