This suggests that when the initial recommendation model provides \qq{a} higher quality initial ranking list (as XSimGCL does), the LLM benefits more from \qq{the} instruction tuning strategies that leverage full ranking contexts.
Comparing \qq{results} across \qq{the} initial recommendation models, we find that stronger initial recommendation models, such as XSimGCL, lead to \qq{a}
