\end{figure}

and $k$ be a sufficiently large natural number. Let $H_{1},\ldots,H_{k}$ be $k$ disjoint copies of $H$. Let $v_1^i$ be the vertex corresponding to $v_1$ in $H$. We construct $H'$ by taking 1-sum of $H_1,H_2,\ldots,H_k$ at $v_1^1,v_1^2,\ldots,v_1^k$, respectively. Let $v_1=v_1^1=v_1^2=\ldots=v_1^k$. We obtain $H''$ by adding an edge $(v_1,v_0)$ to $H'$. See the figure below for an illustration.


