Let $H''_{1},\ldots,H''_{k}$ be $k$ disjoint copies of $H''$. Let $v_0^i$ be the vertex of $H^{''}_i$ corresponding to the vertex $v_0$ of $H''$. Let $G=(V,E)$ be the graph obtained by taking $1-sum$ of $H''_{1},\ldots,H''_{k}$ be at $v_0^1,\ldots,v_0^k$, respectively. Let $v_0=v_0^1=\ldots=v_0^k$. Let $v_{i}$ be the unique neighbor of $v_{0}$ in $H_{i}^{''}$. See the figure below for an illustration.

