From the linearized equations (Eqs. \ref{eq: apx1}, \ref{eq: apx2} and \ref{eq: apx3}) we obtain the Jacobian matrix:

\begin{equation}
\scriptsize
\centerline
{${\mathcal{ J }}(q_n,q_m) = \begin{bmatrix}
    -\frac{8C+Kq^2}{\gamma}& 0 & \frac{q_m}{q^2}(i \beta-\lambda q_n) \\
    0 & -\frac{K q^2}{\gamma} & \frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{q^2}(\beta q_n i -\frac{\lambda}{2}(q_n^2-q_m^2))  \\
